s Data Graph in JSON format\nDescription: You can edit your business data graph in JSON format on the UI.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1328 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Group mapping changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP S/4 HANA Cloud are changed to support the provisioning of application-specific groups.  For more information, see:  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Source)  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Target)  SAP S/4 HANA Cloud (Proxy)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1329 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Intelligent Opportunity Analyzer connector\nDescription: Identity Provisioning supports the Intelligent Opportunity Analyzer connector. You can configure it as source, target, and proxy system for your provisioning scenarios. For more information, see:  Intelligent Opportunity Analyzer (Source)  Intelligent Opportunity Analyzer (Target)  Intelligent Opportunity Analyzer (Proxy)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1330 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-attributes of emails attribute\nDescription: Changes in proxy write transformations of SAP Ariba Category Management and SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management ensure that users with multiple email addresses are provisioned with the correct primary email.  For more information, see: SAP Ariba Category Management and SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",611\n738,\"--- Record 811 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Return Context and Source\nDescription: When creating a new configuration, the context for the reference characteristics and the source of the configuration can be specified. Both, context and source can also be overwritten using the corresponding endpoint.   Context and source used to be missing in the configuration results. Both can now be requested as part of the configuration results by listing them in the $select query parameter like this: $select=context,source.  See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 812 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Return Dependencies That Caused the Conflict\nDescription: Conflicts returned by GET /configurations/{configurationId}dependencyId with a list of dependencies, such as. constraints, that caused the conflict.  See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 813 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Extensions Concept – WHERE LIKE Database Access\nDescription: There is a new API called sap.db() to read table content from local extensions that will support wildcards with LIKE operator in WHERE clauses of SELECT statements.   See Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Production\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 814 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Knowledgebases API – Search By BOM Application\nDescription: There is a new filter value bomApplication for endpoint GET /kbdetermination, which enables the search for knowledge bases by the BOM application, for example SD01 or PP01.   See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 815 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production- Configurations API – Lock Configurations Against Changes\nDescription: There is a new endpoint called PATCH /configurations/{configurationId}/lock to flag a configuration as locked or not locked. The default setting is not locked. If a configuration is locked, it cannot be deleted nor changed, for example, adding or removing a characteristic value or resetting the configuration is not possible.  Existing endpoints such as GET /configurations/{configurationId} will be enhanced to return the locked flag for a configuration.   The existing endpoint GET /externalConfigurations will be enhanced to allow searching for locked configurations.  See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 816 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change in getting Graph service credentials in API consumption for client applications\nDescription: The service plan for enabling client applications has changed. You no longer use the api service plan under SAP 